Relevant columns and how they will be used  

bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr  
• geo_id : 5–digit county FIPS code; join key to vaccination table.  
• total_pop : denominator – latest population estimate.  
• do_date : keep only the most‑recent survey date (2018‑01‑01 for the 2018 5‑yr ACS).  

bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all  
• facility_place_id : unique vaccination‑site ID – count distinct values.  
• facility_sub_region_1 / facility_sub_region_1_code : filter to California ( ‘California’  or  ‘US‑CA’ ).  
• facility_sub_region_2_code : 5–digit county FIPS code – join key to ACS.  

Typical filter / join conditions  
• WHERE do_date = '2018-01-01'  
• WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'                -- or facility_sub_region_1_code = 'US-CA'  
• JOIN … ON LPAD(geo_id,5,'0') = facility_sub_region_2_code  

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Exploratory → progressive → final queries  
(All queries return ≤ 20 rows and are wrapped in ```sql``` blocks.)

```sql
--Description: 1) Inspect all survey dates available in the ACS table.
SELECT DISTINCT do_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`
ORDER BY do_date DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Preview a few California counties’ population records.
SELECT geo_id, total_pop, do_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`
WHERE LPAD(geo_id,5,'0') LIKE '06%'       -- California FIPS prefix
ORDER BY total_pop DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) List the 20 largest CA counties by 2018 population.
SELECT LPAD(geo_id,5,'0') AS county_fips,
       total_pop
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`
WHERE do_date = '2018-01-01'
  AND LPAD(geo_id,5,'0') LIKE '06%'
ORDER BY total_pop DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Check how vaccination records identify the state.
SELECT DISTINCT facility_sub_region_1, facility_sub_region_1_code
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
WHERE facility_sub_region_1_code LIKE 'US-%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Preview vaccination‑site rows for California (any 20).
SELECT facility_place_id,
       facility_name,
       facility_sub_region_2,
       facility_sub_region_2_code
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Count distinct vaccine sites per CA county (top 20 by count).
SELECT facility_sub_region_2_code AS county_fips,
       COUNT(DISTINCT facility_place_id) AS site_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'
GROUP BY county_fips
ORDER BY site_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Show population for those same counties.
SELECT LPAD(geo_id,5,'0') AS county_fips,
       total_pop
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`
WHERE do_date = '2018-01-01'
  AND LPAD(geo_id,5,'0') IN (
        SELECT facility_sub_region_2_code
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
        WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'
        GROUP BY facility_sub_region_2_code )
ORDER BY total_pop DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Join the two tables and compute the raw ratio (not scaled yet).
SELECT p.county_fips,
       p.total_pop,
       v.site_cnt,
       v.site_cnt / p.total_pop AS sites_per_person
FROM (
  SELECT LPAD(geo_id,5,'0') AS county_fips,
         total_pop
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`
  WHERE do_date = '2018-01-01'
    AND LPAD(geo_id,5,'0') LIKE '06%') AS p
JOIN (
  SELECT facility_sub_region_2_code AS county_fips,
         COUNT(DISTINCT facility_place_id) AS site_cnt
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
  WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'
  GROUP BY county_fips) AS v
USING (county_fips)
ORDER BY sites_per_person DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Convert ratio to sites per 1,000 residents and round.
SELECT county_fips,
       site_cnt,
       total_pop,
       ROUND( (site_cnt * 1000) / total_pop , 3) AS sites_per_1000
FROM (
  SELECT p.county_fips,
         p.total_pop,
         v.site_cnt
  FROM (
    SELECT LPAD(geo_id,5,'0') AS county_fips,
           total_pop
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`
    WHERE do_date = '2018-01-01'
      AND LPAD(geo_id,5,'0') LIKE '06%') AS p
  JOIN (
    SELECT facility_sub_region_2_code AS county_fips,
           COUNT(DISTINCT facility_place_id) AS site_cnt
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
    WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'
    GROUP BY county_fips) AS v
  USING (county_fips) )
ORDER BY sites_per_1000 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) FINAL – number of vaccine sites per 1,000 people for every California county.
SELECT
  county_fips,
  MAX(facility_sub_region_2)          AS county_name,
  COUNT(DISTINCT facility_place_id)   AS vaccine_sites,
  SUM(total_pop)                      AS population_2018,
  ROUND( (COUNT(DISTINCT facility_place_id) * 1000.0)
/ SUM(total_pop), 3)                 AS sites_per_1000_pop
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all` AS v
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`                 AS p
  ON LPAD(p.geo_id,5,'0') = v.facility_sub_region_2_code
WHERE v.facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'
  AND p.do_date = '2018-01-01'
GROUP BY county_fips
ORDER BY sites_per_1000_pop DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

Run query #10 to obtain the requested “vaccine sites per 1,000 people” metric for every county in California.
